{%- comment -%}
  Site footer — port of components/layout/site-footer.tsx.

  The column entries are the design's information architecture in full. An entry
  with no URL renders as plain text rather than as a link that would 404 — the
  React version carried that rule against `href: ""` in the content module, and
  a Shopify menu carries it the same way: a link_list the merchant has not
  pointed anywhere yet is simply not rendered as an anchor.

  The newsletter posts to Shopify's own customer form, which is the one thing
  the React version could not do — it rendered a "not connected yet" notice
  instead. That notice is gone because the form now works.

  SOCIALS ARE NO LONGER THIS SECTION'S SETTINGS. They were four generic
  label/URL pairs here until 2026-09-27; they are now three named THEME settings
  read through `snippets/social-links.liquid`, because the same three links also
  render on the home page and the About page and one section's settings cannot
  be read from another section. The snippet's own comment carries the full
  argument and what the move gave up.

  THEY HAVE LOGOS NOW, and this paragraph used to argue the opposite. It said
  they were text "because the design direction asks for minimal icons" and
  because no glyph should be drawn for a trademark. The studio asked for the
  marks directly — "gw mau lengkap sm logo2 nya ya" — and the second half of
  that objection was answered rather than overruled: the glyphs are each
  owner's own official monochrome mark, taken verbatim, not drawn here. See
  `icon.liquid`. The row is still mark-plus-word, not mark alone, so the
  minimal-icons direction survives where it mattered.

  THE GROUND IS A GRADIENT, on instruction 2026-09-22 — "footer dikasih warna
  gradasi sesuai color palette... dari kanan ke kiri" — and it was WIDENED on
  2026-09-27 because the same request came back a second time, which is the
  tell that the first version could not be seen. It could not: `from-brand-light
  to-brand` ran Rocky (#9c8166) to Camel (#725e4c), two browns twelve points of
  lightness apart, which renders as a flat panel unless you are looking for it.
  It now runs `from-brand-light via-brand to-brand-dark` — Rocky at the right
  edge, Camel through the middle, taupe-700 at the left.

  IT WAS WIDENED DOWNWARD, NOT UPWARD, and that is a contrast decision rather
  than a taste one. Cream on the Rocky end already measures 3.36:1, the lowest
  ratio this file accepts anywhere; a lighter stop at that end would have taken
  the footer's own text below it. Every stop added here is DARKER than the old
  ones, so each one improves the ratio. See --color-brand-dark in tokens.css.

  THE AURORA CAME OFF, and that is not a style choice — its `invert` veil is
  hardcoded to `--wl-taupe-900` (`snippets/aurora.liquid`), painted for the
  flat espresso this used to be. `aurora.liquid`'s own comment is explicit
  that the veil "HAS to match the surface underneath: a mismatch shows up as
  a visible rectangle" — exactly the bug that would have shipped here, an
  espresso-coloured box sitting on top of a brown gradient.

  THE BASE TEXT COLOUR MOVED FROM MUTED TO FULL CREAM for the same reason.
  `text-ink-invert-muted` (`--wl-taupe-200`) was calibrated against espresso
  (luminance ~0.01) and reads at best 4.07:1 against this gradient's Camel
  end and as low as 2.43:1 against its lighter Rocky end — both worse than
  what shipped before. Full cream (`text-ink-invert`, `--color-ink-invert`)
  measures 5.63:1 on Camel and 3.36:1 on Rocky — the Rocky-end number is
  exactly the ratio `app/tokens.css` already accepts for Camel-on-cream
  elsewhere in this file, so it is a repeat of a trade-off already made here,
  not a new one. Nothing in the footer sets `-muted` as a resting colour any
  more; the two spots that used it to correct `base.css`'s default anchor
  colour (see their own comments below) now correct it to full cream instead,
  and their hover state is an underline rather than a colour change, because
  cream has no brighter neighbour to hover toward.
{%- endcomment -%}

<footer class="relative isolate overflow-hidden bg-linear-to-l from-brand-light via-brand to-brand-dark text-ink-invert">
  <div class="relative z-10 mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-8 lg:py-section">
    {%- comment -%}
      MOBILE. Stacked one-per-row this footer measured 1053px on a 390x844
      viewport — 1.25 screenfuls, and 23% of the whole home page. So below `lg`
      the link columns go 2-up and the brand block spans both, which measured
      736px. The last column spans the full width too and lays its own links
      2-up: three columns into a 2-up grid otherwise leaves the bottom-right
      cell empty, and an empty cell reads as a missing column rather than as
      space. Measured on the store, not estimated.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-5 gap-y-5 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.4fr)_repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))] lg:gap-block-lg">
      <div class="col-span-2 flex flex-col gap-3 lg:col-span-1 lg:gap-4">
        {% render 'wordmark', on_dark: true, height: 30 %}

        <p class="wl-measure text-caption leading-snug">
          {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.note, label: 'studio note', lines: 2 %}
        </p>

        <div class="mt-2">
          <h2 class="font-display text-h3 text-ink-invert">
            {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.newsletter_heading, label: 'newsletter heading' %}
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-2 wl-measure text-caption leading-snug">
            {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.newsletter_body, label: 'newsletter body', lines: 2 %}
          </p>

          {%- form 'customer', class: 'mt-3 flex items-center gap-2 lg:mt-4 lg:max-w-md' -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="newsletter">
            <label class="sr-only" for="newsletter-email">{{ 'general.email' | t }}</label>
            <input
              id="newsletter-email"
              type="email"
              name="contact[email]"
              required
              placeholder="{{ section.settings.newsletter_placeholder }}"
              class="min-h-11 min-w-0 flex-1 rounded-sm bg-canvas px-4 text-caption text-ink placeholder:text-ink-subtle"
            >
            {%- comment -%}
              `max-w-md` is 448px and the footer is `overflow-hidden`, so on a
              390px screen this button was not merely off the edge — it was
              clipped away and unreachable. It takes its own row below `lg`.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <button
              type="submit"
              class="min-h-11 shrink-0 cursor-pointer rounded-sm bg-brand px-5 text-label uppercase tracking-label text-on-brand transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) hover:bg-brand-hover lg:px-6"
            >
              {{ section.settings.newsletter_cta }}
            </button>
          {%- endform -%}
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        <nav class="flex flex-col gap-2.5 lg:gap-3 {% if forloop.last %}col-span-2 lg:col-span-1{% endif %}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          <h2 class="text-micro uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-invert">{{ block.settings.title }}</h2>
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 lg:gap-2 {% if forloop.last %}max-lg:grid max-lg:grid-cols-2 max-lg:gap-x-5{% endif %}">
            {%- for i in (1..4) -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign label_key = 'link_' | append: i | append: '_label'
                assign url_key = 'link_' | append: i | append: '_url'
                assign entry_label = block.settings[label_key]
                assign entry_url = block.settings[url_key]
              -%}
              {%- if entry_label != blank -%}
                <li>
                  {%- comment -%}
                    An entry with no URL has no page yet, and renders as plain
                    text rather than as a link that would 404. Filling the URL in
                    is the only change needed once the page exists. This is the
                    design's information architecture in full, so the unbuilt
                    destinations stay visible as intent without becoming dead
                    links.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  {%- if entry_url != blank -%}
                    {%- comment -%}
                      Restating the colour here is not decoration. base.css
                      paints every `a` `--color-brand` — correct on cream, and
                      on this footer's Rocky/Camel gradient `--color-brand`
                      IS one of the two gradient stops, so an unstyled link
                      would all but vanish into its own background. The nine
                      entries with no URL are `span`s and inherit the footer's
                      own `text-ink-invert`, so the three real links were the
                      only ones that needed it. Cream has no brighter
                      neighbour to hover toward, so hover is an underline
                      rather than a colour change (2026-09-22, when this
                      moved off `text-ink-invert-muted` — see the section
                      comment above for the contrast numbers).
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <a href="{{ entry_url }}" class="text-caption text-ink-invert underline-offset-4 transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) hover:underline">{{ entry_label }}</a>
                  {%- else -%}
                    <span class="text-caption">{{ entry_label }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </nav>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    <hr class="wl-rule my-block opacity-20">

    {%- comment -%}
      The copyright and the socials share the bottom row and swap to a column
      below `sm`. `flex-wrap` rather than a grid because the social row's width
      depends on how many entries have URLs — one entry and a two-column grid
      leaves a gap where the missing ones were.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 lg:gap-4">
      <p class="text-micro uppercase tracking-nav">{{ section.settings.copyright }}</p>

      {%- comment -%}
        The `nav` wrapper is unconditional and the snippet decides whether there
        is anything inside it — an empty `nav` is invisible and costs nothing,
        whereas counting the URLs here would be the same count the snippet
        already does, kept in step by hand.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <nav aria-label="{{ 'general.social' | t }}">
        {% render 'social-links' %}
      </nav>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Footer",
  "max_blocks": 3,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "note", "label": "Studio note", "default": "Handwoven linen and cotton, sewn in small runs in Bekasi." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Newsletter" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "newsletter_heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Stay in the loop." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "newsletter_body", "label": "Body", "default": "New arrivals, restocks, events, and notes from Wear Label." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "newsletter_placeholder", "label": "Field placeholder", "default": "Enter your email" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "newsletter_cta", "label": "Button", "default": "Subscribe" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Elsewhere" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The Instagram, Shopee and TikTok links beside the copyright are THEME settings now, under Social — not section settings — because the same three links also render on the home page and the About page and must not be three places to edit. This header is kept so nobody goes looking for them here and concludes they were dropped." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Legal" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "copyright", "label": "Copyright", "default": "© 2026 Wear Label." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "column",
      "name": "Link column",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Leave a link's URL empty and it renders as plain text instead of a link that would 404. That is deliberate: the column shows the full information architecture without promising pages that do not exist yet." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "link_1_label", "label": "Link 1" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "link_1_url", "label": "Link 1 URL" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "link_2_label", "label": "Link 2" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "link_2_url", "label": "Link 2 URL" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "link_3_label", "label": "Link 3" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "link_3_url", "label": "Link 3 URL" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "link_4_label", "label": "Link 4" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "link_4_url", "label": "Link 4 URL" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "default": {
    "blocks": [
      { "type": "column", "settings": { "title": "Company" } },
      { "type": "column", "settings": { "title": "My account" } },
      { "type": "column", "settings": { "title": "Customer care" } }
    ]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
